MAOS workspace automation — CI gates, linting, checks

Usage: xtask <COMMAND>

Commands:
  prepush                              Mirror CI drift checks and workspace tests before pushing a story tree
  check-unsafe                         AC2 — Zero-unsafe gate for the capability-validation path
  kloc-check                           AC3 — KLOC budget check with alarm and hard-fail thresholds
  abi-diff                             AC4 — ABI diff against the previous tagged baseline
  check-empty-kernel                   AC6 — I9 structural-state lint for empty-kernel invariant
  check-loom                           AC7 — NFR-Test-9 Loom-not-in-kernel structural grep
  check-service-boundary               AC8 — NFR-Test-2 service-boundary P1–P4 + Spirit-ABI reflection
  check-fr47                           AC2 — FR47 enforcement: vendor LLM SDK dependency scan
  check-security-md                    AC9 — NFR-Ops-4 + FR61 SECURITY.md section gate
  invariant-lock                       AC5 — Invariant lock gate for constitutional amendments
  check-corpus                         AC1 — SHA-256-pinned JSONL corpus verification (NFR-Test-1)
  check-judge-config                   AC2 — Pinned-judge-LLM structural contract (NFR-Test-1)
  clippy-ratchet                       Advisory warning-debt ratchet over a successful cargo-clippy JSON stream
  coverage-matrix                      AC4 — Coverage-matrix delivered-phase enforcement (NFR-Meta-3)
  corpus-staleness                     AC5 — Corpus staleness `valid_until` enforcement (NFR-Meta-2)
  calibrate                            AC6 — Calibration Wilson-CI math (NFR-Aud-8)
  rebaseline-check                     AC3 — Quarterly rebaseline check (NFR-Test-1)
  example-spirit-regen                 Story 2.3 — Template-to-example drift detector and regenerator. DEPRECATED: use `templates-regen` instead
  templates-regen                      Story 7.1 — Generalized template-to-example regenerator (Rust + TS)
  check-a2a-sender-completeness        Story 8.8 AC3 — cross-Host A2A sender-completeness gate: no reference cross-Host sender builds a frame with an unclassified `consent_envelope`
  check-workspace-count                Story 2.5 AC3 — workspace-member-count guard (Cargo.toml vs architecture doc)
  check-kernel-baseline                Story 8.16 §A4 + Story 16-0 — kernel-core single source of truth. Compares `crates/maos-kernel-core/src` against `xtask/kernel-core-baseline.toml` on THREE axes: the `src_lines` count, the pinned file set, and a per-file content hash (so a line-neutral kernel edit reds the gate and the failing file is NAMED). `--emit-pin` prints the paste-ready `[kernel_src]` block
  check-epic-close-coherence           Epic-13 retro C1 — re-derive every epic's roll-up. REDs when an epic is closed over an open story, when a key never advanced, when planning prose disagrees, or when an OPEN epic cites a kernel pin that is not the baseline
  check-exit-commands                  Story 15-3 AC5 — confidence rule 1 made mechanical: every epic's hermetic exit block is tokenised as shell and every `maos`/`maosctl`/ `xtask` verb must exist at HEAD or be owed by a named, open story that actually claims it
  check-model-currency                 Story 17-5 — model-pin currency: every model id pinned in a manifest, the price book or a `main.rs` provider constructor must be current per `xtask/model-currency.toml`. Offline; names `file:line` for each violation
  check-test-cost                      Story 20-12 AC2 — no test compiles the tree: every cargo/rustc/trybuild spawn under a workspace member's tests dir carries `// expensive: <reason>` (tests `#[ignore = "expensive: …"]`, registered in `xtask/test-budgets.toml [[expensive]]` under a job that runs ignored tests) or, for cargo tree/metadata/locate-project/pkgid, `// cargo-query: <reason>`
  check-test-budget                    Story 20-12 AC1 — every test binary in a nextest junit report keeps its Σ per-test time under its `xtask/test-budgets.toml` budget, and the suite under its total; stale `[[exception]]` rows red
  build-test-fixtures                  Story 20-12 AC2 — build every fixture binary/WASM artefact tests resolve (worker fixtures, maosctl, runners, guests, probes) and write `<target>/maos-fixtures/manifest.json` (or an absolute `$MAOS_FIXTURE_DIR`) recording each artefact's `built_at` and source inputs
  gen-termination-corpus               Story 4.1 AC4 — deterministic 1000-scenario termination-corpus generator
  gen-isolation-corpus                 Story 4.5 — deterministic 200-scenario cross-spirit isolation-corpus generator
  check-mock-not-in-release            Story 4.1 A2 — check release binary for forbidden test-double symbols
  check-pub-field-constructors         Epic 4 retro §A4 — pub fields with `Construct via ::new` doc-attr MUST have a matching `::new` impl
  check-composition-root-completeness  Epic 4 retro §A5 — every `*Adapter` re-exported from `api.rs` MUST be constructed exactly once in `main.rs`
  check-multi-provider-drift           Story 5.5b — multi-provider drift check across aggregated reports
  check-serde-error-handling           Epic 5 retro §A3 (closes Epic 4 retro §A6) — flag `.unwrap_or_default()` / `.unwrap()` / `.expect(...)` after serde calls
  check-review-findings-resolved       Epic 5 retro §A5 — open Review Findings rows MUST block sprint-status `done`; closed rows MUST reference a File List entry
  check-dev-record-completeness        Epic 5 retro §A6 (closes Epic 4 retro §A7) — `done` stories MUST have non-TBD model + non-empty dev record + File List files in `git diff`
  check-manifest-schema-version        Epic 6 §A4 (retro 2026-05-28) — keep MANIFEST_SCHEMA_VERSION + MIN/MAX constants self-consistent and ban hardcoded `manifest_schema_version` comparisons in `maos-manifest` production code
  check-skill-schema                   Story 7.4 — assert the maos.skill.v1 schema posture: valid round-trip + deny_unknown_fields (UnknownField, not a silent default) + semver validation
  check-dev-model-tier                 Epic 12 retro B3 — frontier-era (epic >= 12) stories must record an allowlisted dev model + a §A6 review artifact (Blocking; closes E11-A1)
  check-decision-register              Story 14-0 AC1 — the Epic-14 preflight decision register gets a READER. Every row's target must resolve to a `development_status` key (`epic-*` keys and retro actions are not vehicles); an OPEN row whose mechanical deadline has passed REDS; a non-mechanical deadline must declare itself UNQUERYABLE. Fails closed on an unreadable/unparseable/empty register
  check-j1-loopback-delegation         j1-crosshost-1a AC4 — the J1 `developer-remote` delegation must be provably FRAME-BORNE. Proven-red leg: any "route locally anyway" regression reds this. Boundary leg: loopback `frame.from.host_id` is unverified until rung 2
  check-j1-two-host-signed-run         j1-crosshost-2c AC5.1 — the two-host signed run's judge. Holds the controls that decide what a signed two-host artifact may assert: the signing-identity repair, the host discriminator under the signature, a reconciliation that refuses one root, an enforced bundle schema, typed+bounded faults, nothing `Duplicate` until durable, pin refusals journaled both sides, and a stored-row scan. ONE binding class; the paid run is a validated capture
  stability-matrix                     Story 7.5a — generate (or `--check`) repo-root STABILITY.md from live workspace state (ABI Stability Triple + LTS + compliance/export STUBs)
  check-breaking-md                    Story 7.5a — enforce BREAKING.md dated-entry taxonomy (NFR-Maint-7)
  check-dependency-closure             Story 10.4a — dependency-closure gate (kernel-core artifact excludes Postgres/pgvector)
  check-host-surface                   Story 11.1a — maos-host public-API baseline gate (ADR-031 Spirit Host Port); removed items RED, added items reported but GREEN
  check-rto-gate                       Story 10.4a — RTO ≤ 4h gate (drilled, not printed); NFR-Ops-9
  rto-drill                            Story 10.4a — RTO ≤ 4h drill: performs cold-restore + timing, gates on threshold, and writes evidence consumed by `check-rto-gate`. NFR-Ops-2 (RTO) + NFR-Ops-1 (RPO), drilled not printed
  nfr-onb-1-gate                       Story 7.5b — NFR-Onb-1 30-Minute First Spirit Validation Gate discipline rail: stratification + cohort evaluator + Butler-corpus seam over the committed example cohort/outcomes/self-trial; FAILs loudly on drift
  cassette-age-gate                    Story 8.15 — cassette age gate: fail if any cassette's recorded_at exceeds 14 days
  check-env-contract                   Story 8.15 — env-contract gate: every MAOS_* env::var read must be registered
